benvida.titulo = Welcome to the Lúa installer
benvida.desc = This wizard will guide you through installing Lúa, Piztu's report generator (the paperwork of school departments: annual schedule and minutes, with a style of its own for each centre and PDF export through LaTeX). You can close it and continue later.
benvida.que.titulo = 📅  What is Lúa?
benvida.que.sub = Department reports, in your centre's style
benvida.que.corpo = Lúa produces the paperwork of any teaching department: the annual schedule (you add each month's tasks) and the department's monthly minutes with the subject follow-up reports. It is compiled with LaTeX, and the design and fixed texts of each document live in the template. Each centre can have its own template (logo, name, phone numbers…) and export to PDF, LaTeX, Markdown, Word and OpenDocument.
benvida.deps.titulo = 📦  Dependencies it will install
benvida.deps.sub = The LaTeX toolchain (not texlive-full)
benvida.deps.corpo = • pdflatex, xelatex and lualatex (LaTeX engines)\n• TikZ (vector drawings) and poppler-utils (preview)\n\nIt is a few hundred MB, not several GB: only the packages Lúa really uses are picked.
benvida.modulo.titulo = 🧩  Integrates with Piztu
benvida.modulo.sub = Shows up in ⚙ Classroom → Modules
benvida.modulo.corpo = If Piztu is already installed on this machine, Lúa hooks itself into its module selector automatically. If it isn't, Lúa still works fine as a standalone app.
benvida.aviso = ⚠️  To install into /opt/piztu/modulos and create shortcuts, run the installer with sudo.

inst.card = Step 1 — Installation
inst.desc = This step:\n• Copies Lúa's files to %s (Piztu's modules folder, so it already shows up in its selector)\n• Installs the LaTeX toolchain (pdflatex/xelatex/lualatex, TikZ, poppler-utils)\n• Presets Lúa to this installation's language
inst.out.inicial = Press the button to start the installation...
inst.btn = 🚀 Install Lúa
inst.iniciando = Starting installation...\n
inst.erro = \n❌ Error: %s
inst.ok = \n✅ Installation complete! Continue to the next step.
inst.log.extraendo = 📁 Extracting files to %s…
inst.log.extraidos = ✅ Files extracted\n
inst.log.deps = 📦 Installing LaTeX (this can take several minutes)…
inst.log.depsok = ✅ LaTeX installed\n
inst.log.depsfail = ⚠️  Could not install all dependencies: %s\n    You can retry later from Lúa → Options.

fin.card = ✅  Lúa installed successfully!
fin.desc = Lúa was installed into %s.\n\nIf you have Piztu (piztu) installed, open it and look for Lúa under ⚙ Classroom → Modules.\n\nCreate shortcuts to launch Lúa from the desktop:
fin.btn = 🖥️  Create shortcuts
fin.erro = ❌ Error: %s
fin.creados = ✅ Shortcuts created:\n• Application menu (Education → Lúa)\n• Desktop (Lúa)

desinst.titulo = ⚠️  Danger zone
desinst.intro = This action undoes the installation and cannot be reversed.
desinst.card = 🗑️  Uninstall Lúa
desinst.desc = Removes /opt/piztu/modulos/lua (including personal settings and any saved AI keys), the shortcuts and the icon.
desinst.deps.label = Also uninstall LaTeX (system packages; other programs might use them)
desinst.palabra = UNINSTALL
desinst.confirmar.label = Type %s to confirm
desinst.btn = 🗑️  Uninstall Lúa
desinst.confirm = This will completely remove Lúa from this machine, including personal settings. This cannot be undone. Continue?
desinst.erro = \n❌ Error: %s
desinst.ok = \n✅ Lúa fully uninstalled.

# ── macOS variants ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Keys ending in ".darwin" replace the base key when the installer runs
# on a Mac (see aplicarVariantesSO, i18n.go).
benvida.aviso.darwin = ⚠️  The Applications folder is not writable. Log in with an administrator account (do not use sudo: Homebrew refuses to run as root).
benvida.deps.sub.darwin = Installed with Homebrew
benvida.deps.corpo.darwin = • Homebrew (the macOS package manager; installed if you don't have it)\n• MacTeX (pdflatex, xelatex, lualatex and TikZ)\n• poppler (preview) and pandoc (export to Word/ODT)\n\nMacTeX is several GB and takes a while. You will be asked for the administrator password only for that step.
benvida.modulo.titulo.darwin = 🍎  Native macOS application
benvida.modulo.sub.darwin = Installed into Applications
benvida.modulo.corpo.darwin = Lúa is installed as /Applications/Lua.app, so it shows up in Launchpad and Spotlight like any other app. Piztu is a Linux-based system for schools and does not exist on macOS, so here Lúa always runs as a standalone application.
inst.desc.darwin = This step:\n• Installs Lúa into %s\n• Installs Homebrew (if needed) and MacTeX\n• Presets Lúa to this installation's language
fin.desc.darwin = Lúa was installed into %s.\n\nYou can now open it from Launchpad or Spotlight. Press the button to register it with the system so it shows up right away:
fin.btn.darwin = 🍎  Register Lúa with the system
fin.creados.darwin = ✅ Lúa registered:\n• Launchpad and Spotlight\n• Applications folder
desinst.desc.darwin = Removes /Applications/Lua.app (including personal settings and any saved AI keys) and unregisters it from the system.
desinst.deps.label.darwin = Also uninstall MacTeX from Homebrew (other programs might use it)
